{"name":"Privileged Elite","hex":"#597695","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"privileged","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of privilege"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having special privileges.","Not subject to legal discovery due to a protected status."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/privileged"},{"term":"elite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of high birth or social position; aristocratic or patrician.","Representing the choicest or most select of a group."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A special group or social class of people who have a superior social or economic status and attendant power, advantages, or privileges in society; a member of such a group.","An individual member of such a group."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elite","blocks":[{"text":"In political and sociological theory, the elite are a small group of powerful or wealthy people who hold a disproportionate amount of wealth, privilege, political power, or skill in a group. Defined by the Cambridge Dictionary, the \"elite\" are \"the richest, most powerful, best-educated, or best-trained group in a society\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Prime_Minister_Boris_Johnson_UNGA_visit_%2851786182369%29.jpg/330px-Prime_Minister_Boris_Johnson_UNGA_visit_%2851786182369%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elite","wikidata":"Q192797"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg/500px-Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg/1280px-Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=par